        {
          "_key": "l5pk",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/safety/data-and-statistics/large-truck-and-bus-crash-facts-2020"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5pj",
          "text": "According to the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5pl",
          "text": "Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration",
          "marks": [
            "l5pk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5pm",
          "text": ", in 2020, 156 buses were involved in fatal crashes throughout the United States. This included 86 transit buses, 46 school buses and 9 intercity buses. While this represents the lowest number since FARS data collecting began in 1975, it excludes the thousands of bus accidents that were not fatal. Bus accidents can cause serious and catastrophic injuries to those involved, including:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
